Optional SSSP v2.0 pseudopotential collections

Run from the CP2K repository root to install PBE Efficiency
python3 tools/pseudopotentials/fetch_sssp.py data/SSSP/2.0 --install --library pbe-eff

Select pbe-eff, pbe-prec, pbesol-eff or pbesol-prec with --library.
Repeat --library to select several collections. Omit it to install all four.
Each collection contains 95 original UPF files and its original cutoffs.json.
Files are installed under {pbe,pbesol}/{efficiency,precision} without changes.
New archives are removed after installation. Existing files are reused only
when their contents match. Calculation startup does not download files.

Set DIRECTORY to another writable data location if preferred. For example
python3 tools/pseudopotentials/fetch_sssp.py "$CP2K_DATA_DIR/SSSP/2.0" --install --library pbe-prec

Source repository
https://github.com/unkcpz/sssp-verify-scripts
Source revision
0fb07d89d13407b0f00a0a3b8c21d7e387fb56f9

The archive URLs and SHA-256 checksums are recorded in
tools/pseudopotentials/sssp_v2_archives.json at the CP2K repository root.
tools/pseudopotentials/fetch_sssp.py retrieves the same pinned archives.

The cutoff files contain the upstream plane-wave recommendations. They do
not prescribe a Gaussian basis or Quickstep multigrid settings.
Calculation support depends on the pseudopotential type, method and basis.

